# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw FitBit data — 604 MB, and several files exceed GitHub's limits.
# GitHub blocks any file over 100 MB and warns above 50 MB. These are the
# worst offenders:
#     heartrate_seconds_merged.csv      86 MB / 40 MB
#     minuteCaloriesNarrow_merged.csv   70 MB / 64 MB
#     minuteMETsNarrow_merged.csv       50 MB / 46 MB
#
# The data is CC0 and one click away on Kaggle, so there is no reason to
# commit it. The README tells people where to get it.
#     https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/arashnic/fitbit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mturkfitbit_export_*/
*.zip

# If you DO want the small daily-level files tracked, delete the two lines
# above and use these instead — they keep dailyActivity/sleepDay/weightLog
# and drop only the huge minute- and second-level files:
#
# mturkfitbit_export_*/**/minute*.csv
# mturkfitbit_export_*/**/heartrate_seconds_merged.csv

# ---- R ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj

# knitr / rmarkdown intermediates
*_cache/
*_files/
*.knit.md
*.utf8.md

# ---- Python / Jupyter ------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/

# ---- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
